      "title": "UI as a projection over context in agentic systems",
      "summary": "Researchers propose AFS-UI, a framework that reconceptualises user interfaces as dynamic projections over context built on agentic systems, moving away from fragmented request-response pipelines.",
      "key_facts": [
        "Proposes AFS-UI framework for generative user interfaces",
        "Reconceptualises UI as projections over context in agentic systems",
        "Addresses limitations of traditional request-response generative pipelines"
      ],
      "design_implication": "When designing interfaces driven by autonomous agent workflows, static layouts often break down the moment context shifts or multi-step execution branches. Relying on fixed component libraries leaves users guessing about the underlying state during long-horizon tasks. Start treating layouts as dynamic projections over live execution context, ensuring that interface components adapt their structure transparently as the underlying agent gathers new information.",
      "implication_lens": "pattern",
      "visual_need": "illustrate",
      "source_name": "arXiv cs.HC",
