      "title": "Ambiguity in AI memory permissions and preview rules",
      "summary": "A new research study investigates what people can infer about saved memory rules when presented with limited preview examples of allowed and blocked assistant actions.",
      "key_facts": [
        "Evaluates ambiguity in AI memory permissions and preview rules",
        "Examines user inference from single allowed and blocked action previews",
        "Analyzes rule compatibility for editors with multiple valid rules"
      ],
      "design_implication": "In settings where AI assistants retain cross-session memory, users frequently struggle to predict the exact boundaries of automated recall based on simple allow-or-block examples. Ambiguous permission rules lead to unexpected data exposure during routine interactions. Start designing explicit memory audit logs that display full rule implications rather than isolated test previews, so users can verify exactly what context an agent is allowed to retain.",
      "implication_lens": "trust_and_risk",
      "visual_need": "illustrate",
      "source_name": "arXiv cs.HC",
      "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.17874",
